-- M9 s2: the credential circuit (docs/M9-PLAN.md D1). A holder has an
-- attribute attr and a spend key sk. The commitment is cm = poseidon([attr,
-- sk]) and the nullifier is nf = poseidon([sk, scope]). Public: cm, nf, the
-- scope and the threshold min. Private: attr, sk and the difference d.
-- The attribute check is d + min == attr with range8 d: a lookup of d in
-- the table 0 to 255. This is a relation in the field. It gives the integer
-- bound min <= attr <= min + 255 only when min <= r - 256 (r is the BN254
-- scalar modulus): min = r - 1, attr = 0, d = 1 satisfies both constraints.
-- The consumer contract must refuse a policy with min > r - 256 (D7).
-- Each hash has the form (i) of examples/poseidon.glue: one hint for each
-- S-box output and each state word, and one constraint for each hint. The
-- hints of the nullifier hash start with n (ntRkJ, nsRkI), the hints of the
-- commitment hash start with c (ctRkJ, csRkI). The constants and sbox5 are
-- the defs of examples/poseidon.lang.
